 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? A balanced meal of protein, carbs and fruit is the key. Think sandwiches, fruit and yogurt, and keep easy things like cheese and crackers next to the kitchen. Yellow food is lots of bananas, eggs and toast. Add little things like cheese, biscuits or crisps for energy. Coffee is fine, but try add some milk or yogurt with some fruit too. Some kids don't like cereal, so try toasting some bread with butter and banana sliced on top. Letting her have small role, even just helping with the vegetables, makes it feel less like chore.",
